<title>UK: Lehman sets 175 bln lire Aug 2002 structured bond.</title>
<headline>Lehman sets 175 bln lire Aug 2002 structured bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers BCI, Cariplo and Lehman.</p>
<p> BORROWER   LEHMAN BROTHERS HOLDING PLC</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  LEHMAN BROTHERS HOLDING PLC</p>
<p> AMT    175 BLN LIRE  COUPON    *7.30	MATURITY    01.AUG.02</p>
<p> TYPE    FIXED/FRN    ISS PRICE  101.675   PAY DATE    01.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	 =</p>
<p> NOTES	*FOR FIRST YEAR THEN COUPON BECOMES 7.0 PCT OR SWITCHES</p>
<p>		 TO FRN PAYING SEMI-ANNUAL LIRE LIBOR +0.375 PCT -</p>
<p>		 AT ISSUERS OPTION.</p>
<p> MOODY	BAA1	LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A	   DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  MGT/UND    0.625     SELL CONC  1.25</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
